# get_up — success
#
# GET UP exists only in the get-up phase, which follows the childhood reminescences — so like
# cli/remember/, this test must NOT pass --skip-childhood, the flag every other script in the suite
# uses. That is why the verb had no test.
#
# Reaching it means playing the whole childhood out: five reminescences, each a full
# observe -> think -> remember chain plus the result's CONTINUE to move to the next. The loop below
# is those five, unrolled — the count and the fragments are fixed by --seed 42. A script has no
# repetition, and unrolling reads better than pretending otherwise.
#
# The get-up is played on the same ground: "Myself" now holds the three states of the body's
# exhaustion, what stands around may be looked at, and whatever is thought about, the thought ends on
# rising. The phase skips the critic and forces difficulty 1, so failure loops back with no penalty
# rather than costing anything — there is no meaningful fail.cli, and cli/get_up/ has one script
# deliberately.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60

# ── The five childhood reminescences ─────────────────────────────────────────
advance 12 180
click observe "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 12 180

click observe "manure smelt"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "manure smelt"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 12 180

click observe "nothing"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "nothing"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 12 180

click observe "a dirty traveller"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a dirty traveller"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 12 180

click observe "shelter"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "shelter"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# ── The get-up phase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
wait mode GetUp 60
# Waking is a break in the music, as entering the childhood was: the get-up's own mood, sparse.
expect-state music tracks=2 filter=None cold=0.60 fear=0.15 mystery=0.15
advance 12 180
regions

# The childhood's branches went with the childhood; the scenery answers now.
expect-no-state trees "a scream"
expect-state symbols click observe thing
expect-no-state symbols "(disabled)"

strategy succeed
click observe "aching legs"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "aching legs"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
regions

# Before and after, because the phase's one silent failure is that it pays the chain nothing.
# The practice loop in CommitOutcomeResult used to sit inside its `deferredCommit` branch, and
# Get-Up is the ONLY caller that commits synchronously — so it rolled dice against the chain's
# levels, narrated the outcome, and awarded no experience at all. Nothing caught it: `inspect
# skills` reported the level only, and a level takes several successes to move.
inspect skills
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180
inspect skills

# What makes this a get_up test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb get_up

# The two halves of what a successful act owes, and they are different outcomes:
#   vigor    — the lesson the verb teaches of itself (ModusMentisGrantOutcome), newly known here
#   ripelore — a point of practice to a modus mentis that carried the chain, and it stood at xp=0
#              before the action, so the whole of this value was earned by THIS phase
# Both values are pinned by --seed 42, as everything in this script is; if the childhood content
# changes the chain, this fails naming the skill, which is the right way to be told.
expect-state skills skill vigor level=1 xp=0
expect-state skills skill ripelore level=1 xp=1

# And the first sight of the world is a second break, into the map's music. The phase ends on the
# result's CONTINUE, as each reminescence did.
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
expect-state music tracks=4 filter=None cold=0.65 fear=0.60
quit
